<!--
TEMPLATE: substitute the tokens listed below.

Substitution tokens:
  <<DATE>>                  — YYYY-MM-DD of the run
  <<RUN_ID>>                — short identifier unique within this skill (UUID suffix recommended to prevent collisions when concurrent runs overlap)
  <<SKILL>>                 — skill name being scheduled (matches the parent skill folder)
  <<OUTCOME>>               — success | partial | failure
  <<DURATION_MIN>>          — integer minutes the run took
  <<AUTHORITY_DECLARED>>    — bracketed list copied from PROCESS.md `authority:` at run time
  <<AUTHORITY_USED>>        — bracketed list of actions actually taken (best-effort; v1 may equal declared)
  <<VERIFICATION_STATE>>    — `unverified` on first run; a human edits to `verified` after reviewing output
  <<PROPOSED_DELTA>>        — free text describing a suggested change to SKILL.md/PROCESS.md, or "none"
  <<STATUS>>                — open | applied | rejected

Convention:
  Scheduled runs write to `<skill-folder>/scheduled-runs/` — NEVER to `history/`.
  Manual invocations (interactive Claude Code session) write to `history/` instead.
  This file is the per-run-record schema for the scheduled folder. The body below
  the frontmatter is free-form prose (notes, links, decisions, observed authority
  drift, etc.).
-->

---
date: <<DATE>>
run_id: <<RUN_ID>>
skill: <<SKILL>>
triggered_by: schedule
outcome: <<OUTCOME>>
duration_min: <<DURATION_MIN>>
authority_declared: <<AUTHORITY_DECLARED>>
authority_used: <<AUTHORITY_USED>>
verification_state: <<VERIFICATION_STATE>>
proposed_delta: <<PROPOSED_DELTA>>
status: <<STATUS>>
---

# scheduled run — <<SKILL>> @ <<DATE>>

## Context

What this scheduled run was supposed to accomplish (1-2 sentences). Free-form prose; the structured signal lives in the frontmatter above.

## What happened

Step-by-step or paragraph summary. If the run took an action OUTSIDE the declared authority list, document the refusal here (the prelude-injected self-check should have caught it, but a human reviewer scanning this section is the v1 backstop until the v2 post-run guard ships).

## Outcome

One-line restatement matching `outcome:` in the frontmatter. If `partial` or `failure`, name the failure mode.

## Notes

Anything worth surfacing to the owner agent's next process-improvement pass — friction, drift between `authority_declared:` and `authority_used:`, suggestions for `proposed_delta:`, links to artifacts produced or issues filed.
